          "text": "**Clinical Indication:**  \nPatient with combined generalized and focal epilepsy, clinically characterized by generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 39, occurring approximately 5 times per month. Etiology is genetic, associated with an **STXBP1 c.902A>G** variant. Seizures are drug-resistant. Current antiseizure medications are oxcarbazepine and valproate.\n\n**Technique:**  \nRoutine scalp EEG performed using standard international 10–20 electrode placement with bipolar and referential montages.\n\n**Findings:**  \nSpecific background, interictal, and ictal EEG findings are not provided in the authorized clinical information.\n\n**Impression:**  \nRoutine EEG interpretation is limited because electrographic findings are not available in the provided data. Clinical history is notable for drug-resistant combined generalized and focal epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures, genetic etiology associated with an **STXBP1 c.902A>G** variant.",
